{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Declaring Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Declaring Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"],"anchor":"Declaring-Systems"},{"title":"System Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"],"anchor":"System-Parameters"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A system is a type with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method that a schedule calls once per run. The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro turns a structure into a system from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Each parameter’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type says what part of the world the system works on and whether it reads or writes it, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":" is always exact, and a schedule can run systems that don’t conflict at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Read-and-Write-Components","level":3,"text":"Read and Write Components","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Take a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to read components, and iterate it as you would a world’s query"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"results. Take an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to change them in place. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"update can also read other components with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Over"},{"type":"text","text":", and narrow the entities it visits with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Where"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct Climb {","    func run(_ climbers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        climbers { position, row in","            position.y += abs(row.components.dy)","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let climber = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: -3))","let statue = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 0, dy: -3), Frozen())","Schedule { Climb() }.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: climber].y)","\/\/ Prints \"3.0\"","print(world[Position.self, of: statue].y)","\/\/ Prints \"0.0\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Climb"},{"type":"text","text":" writes "},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and reads "},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Frozen"},{"text":". It conflicts with any system that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Frozen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or reads or writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":", and runs at the same time as any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"other."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parameter’s filter is a list of filter types in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Where"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/With"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Without"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Added"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Changed"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Allows"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/AnyOf"},{"type":"text","text":" of filter types. Each mirrors the query filter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the same name."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two parameters that name the same component, one of them writing it, are a compile-time error."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"A conflict the macro can’t see by name, such as one through a type alias, traps when a schedule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes the system.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Read-and-Write-Resources-and-Events","level":3,"text":"Read and Write Resources and Events","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a resource and a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" changes one. An "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends events, and an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads the events sent since the system last read them. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"following schedule sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Damage"},{"type":"text","text":" event for each entity below the ground, then applies the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"damage to its target’s health:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: -1), Health(current: 30))","","let frame = Schedule {","    UpdateEvents()","    Combat()","    ApplyDamage().after(Combat.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","print(world[Health.self, of: knight].current)","\/\/ Prints \"20\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" declares "},{"code":"Combat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader"},{"text":" declares ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplyDamage"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Spawn-and-Despawn-Entities","level":3,"text":"Spawn and Despawn Entities","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A system that runs alongside others can’t spawn or despawn entities directly, because that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"changes every component type at once. Take an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},{"text":" instead, and queue","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the changes. Commands apply at the end of the wave the system runs in, so systems ordered after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it see them:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@System","struct RemoveDefeated {","    func run(_ fighters: Query<Health>, _ commands: inout Commands) {","        for (entity, health) in fighters where health.current <= 0 {","            commands.despawn(entity)","        }","    }","}","","var world = World()","let knight = world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 12))","Schedule { RemoveDefeated() }.run(on: &world)","","print(world.contains(knight))","\/\/ Prints \"false\"","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A commands parameter conflicts with nothing, so it doesn’t stop a system from running at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same time as others."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Take-the-Whole-World","level":3,"text":"Take the Whole World","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method that takes ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout World","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes a system that can change anything. Its access is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a schedule runs it alone, after the systems written before it and before those written","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after it. Use one for work that touches many types at once, such as loading a level.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To write a system by hand instead of with the macro, conform a type to "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"type":"text","text":", implement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and declare an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"type":"text","text":" listing every type the system reads and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Run-on-the-Main-Actor","level":3,"text":"Run on the Main Actor","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mark a system type, or its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":" to make a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"},{"type":"text","text":", which a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule runs on the main actor after the other systems of its wave. Use one to carry results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the world to a user interface."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you’ve declared systems, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to order them and run them only when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a condition holds."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/With":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/With","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"With"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"With"}],"title":"With","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A filter type that passes the entities holding a component of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/with"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface."}],"title":"MainActorSystem","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs."}],"title":"System","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Without":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Without","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/without","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Without"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Without"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Without","abstract":[{"text":"A filter type that passes the entities holding no component of type ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Added":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Added","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Added","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Added","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Added","abstract":[{"text":"A filter type that passes the entities whose component of type ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" was added since the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world’s last run.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/added"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Update","abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/AnyOf":{"role":"symb